<title>FINLAND: Finnish July EU-harmonised CPI up 1.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Finnish July EU-harmonised CPI up 1.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish consumer price index harmonised to European Union standards rose 1.1 percent year-on-year in July after a 1.1 percent rise in June, Statistics Finland (SF) said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>			     July 1997	June 1997     July 1996</p>
<p> Yr/Yr			+1.1 pct	 +1.1 pct	+1.1 pct</p>
<p> Mth/Mth		    -0.2 pct	 +0.2 pct	-0.2 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1996=100)   101.2	    101.4	   102.3</p>
<p>According to SF's regular national method of calculation, Finnish consumer prices were unchanged in July on June and rose 1.2 percent year-on-year, it said. @</p>
<p>			     July 1997	June 1997     July 1996</p>
<p> Yr/yr			+1.2 pct	 +1.2 pct	+0.5 pct</p>
<p> Mth/mth		    -0.0 pct	 +0.2 pct	-0.1 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1990=100)   114.2	    114.2	   112.8</p>
<p>Six economists' average forecast for the national CPI figure had been for a 1.3 percent rise year-on-year and a 0.1 percent rise month-on-month.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
